			title: "&fThe Drawer Wall"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["57D0000000000002"]
			description: [
				"A &eCompacting Drawer&r holds one material in every size at once - nuggets, ingots and blocks share the same slot and convert as you take them. One drawer, the whole iron economy."
				""
				"&e&lWhy this beats three ordinary drawers.&r A normal drawer holding iron ingots fills up and starts voiding or backing up your system. A Compacting Drawer silently converts overflow &lupward&r - 9 ingots become a block, 9 blocks become... nothing further, but you have just multiplied your effective capacity ninefold without a single upgrade."
				""
				"&7Pull from the nugget face and it breaks a block down for you automatically. Insert blocks and it stores them as ingots. You never manually compress anything again.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe catch:&r one material per drawer, and only materials that have a real nugget/ingot/block chain. Iron, gold, copper, osmium, all the Mekanism metals - yes. Cobblestone or gravel - no, use an ordinary drawer."
				""
				"&8Put these on your ore output line first. Metals are what actually overflow in this pack; everything else is a rounding error by comparison."
			]
			icon: "storagedrawers:compacting_drawers_3"
			id: "57D0000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "57D0000000000104"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Nugget, ingot, block - one slot"
			tasks: [{
				id: "57D0000000000203"
				item: "storagedrawers:compacting_drawers_3"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&fCompacting Drawers"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["57D0000000000003"]
			description: [
				"The &eDrawer Controller&r turns the whole wall into one block: shift-click it and everything in your inventory flies into its matching drawer."
				""
				"Come home, dump, done. Pipes and hoppers can feed it too."
			]
